type of bignums should be integer, not T.

(type-of (fact 100))
--> T ; too vague

(type-of (fact 100))
--> INTEGER ; better

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIXED in v1.4.44.

sources/bocl.c kernel_TYPE_OF() handled fixnums (integerp -> (INTEGER lo hi)) but
had no case for out-of-fixnum-range numbers, so a bignum, a ratio and a complex
all fell through to the catch-all T.  Added:
  - bignum  -> INTEGER
  - ratio   -> RATIO
  - complex -> COMPLEX
consistent with TYPEP ((type-of x) is a type of which x is a member: a bignum is
INTEGER/RATIONAL/NUMBER, a ratio is RATIO/RATIONAL, a complex is COMPLEX/NUMBER).

  (type-of (fact 100))  =>  INTEGER   ; was T

Regression test: tests/test_slice22.c test_type_of.  Full suite green.
